<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Release-only entitlements for DynaMoE.

    keychain-access-groups moves the app onto the data protection keychain
    (SecretStoreSupport.swift), which authorizes items by this group instead of a
    per-item ACL. That is what stops macOS from asking for keychain access again
    whenever a new version is installed.

    Two properties of this entitlement are easy to get wrong:

    1. It is a restricted entitlement. It only works alongside an embedded
       Developer ID provisioning profile that grants RMY84Y8G7M.*, which is why
       the Release configuration is MANUALLY signed with the "Developer ID
       Application" identity and PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER = "DynaMoE
       Developer ID". Xcode refuses automatic signing with a Developer ID
       identity, and an app that carries this entitlement without a matching
       profile is killed by launchd at startup. A missing profile therefore has
       to fail the BUILD, not the launch, so install it first:
       `Tools/install_profile.py <file.provisionprofile>` validates the profile
       against the certificate this Mac actually holds, copies it into both
       provisioning directories and removes older profiles with the same name.
       That is the only supported path: manual signing with a profile specifier
       means `xcodebuild -allowProvisioningUpdates` cannot resolve a profile by
       name for you. Debug is unaffected.

    2. $(AppIdentifierPrefix) is expanded by Xcode. codesign expands nothing, so
       any hand-written signing step must use the literal group instead:
       RMY84Y8G7M.DRP.DynaMoE.

    The Debug configuration deliberately has no keychain group
    (DynaMoE-Debug.entitlements): the entitlement forces profile resolution at
    build time and would otherwise break the fast local loop, and an unentitled
    build already falls back to the legacy keychain.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)DRP.DynaMoE</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
